{"id": "EUVD-2026-93329", "enisaUuid": "4fdb47e6-e380-315e-8dfa-3e04099543d9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: Fix device kref underflow in dma_chan_put()\n\ndma_chan_get() takes chan->device->ref only on the slow path:\n\n\t/* no kref on fast path */\n\tif (chan->client_count) {\n\t\t__module_get(owner);\n\t\tchan->client_count++;\n\t\treturn 0;\n\t}\n\tif (!try_module_get(owner))\n\t\treturn -ENODEV;\n\tif (!dma_device_get(chan->device)) { // calls kref_get_unless_zero()\n\ndma_chan_put() drops the ref unconditionally, so every fast-path\nget/put pair drops one extra device reference.\n\nThe bug fires when two conditions hold together: a non-private\nprovider has a persistent client holding chan->client_count > 0\nand another client cycles dmaengine_get()/dmaengine_put().\nWhen the kref hits zero, the subsequent dma_find_channel() returns\nNULL even though the provider module is still loaded.\n\nFix this by dropping device->ref only on the last put, matching the\nsingle slow-path get.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/036b527f92570206da4b8c40b38f8d689e29d0f3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5fb1797a8c9485e40e5492fa0338ab5c7d1f3fef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/57f7f1c6827be7d8f80feca48d2125fb91c6f6ed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c3f4ce651d43705f9ec7f778f642a90d5ff4fba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/de2677e57d3161390d8a508f08cddec6ef7e4b23", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a0d9b406febf23054ad595fd47b29325e70fb2d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77906ac448d2fa81fa710ae26c0e591ebdc81154", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/44dab659064eb5c10adb0306510eebe848ed592d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98344", "GHSA-g4c2-fm3r-x4gh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "098e89fa-2439-399f-a393-1431bfd5819b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ad342a863590b24ce77681b7e081363fb3333f7 <036b527f92570206da4b8c40b38f8d689e29d0f3"}, {"id": "1d62cd09-8408-3c69-904e-d353e43e58b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1d7bc2f1-04f0-3c41-aa00-971810e05232", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ad342a863590b24ce77681b7e081363fb3333f7 <5fb1797a8c9485e40e5492fa0338ab5c7d1f3fef"}, {"id": "2242dc19-059f-33ec-b897-2cd09613aef2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ad342a863590b24ce77681b7e081363fb3333f7 <de2677e57d3161390d8a508f08cddec6ef7e4b23"}, {"id": "338dec34-f6c9-324b-b55a-6960ca97a5c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "3de0e9fc-8a68-39c9-9b79-5ca7e9cf2584", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "4788a974-7306-322b-abf3-e9128652b045", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.6"}, {"id": "4ddfc1db-af85-354b-8ab7-d4fca1e3bb12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "56a93aec-93c7-3c4a-bfaf-80b598e094c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ad342a863590b24ce77681b7e081363fb3333f7 <7c3f4ce651d43705f9ec7f778f642a90d5ff4fba"}, {"id": "b179c72f-f910-3659-9f42-d4437d326178", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b4e92644-a21b-3adb-b943-5ab5e3aa4927", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "b54748e5-b13e-380a-9064-e54b9ac5a176", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ad342a863590b24ce77681b7e081363fb3333f7 <1a0d9b406febf23054ad595fd47b29325e70fb2d"}, {"id": "b75a2dba-4562-340d-8dfb-e5105cc5c343", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "bf0e014e-33cc-39a9-a7e4-5b1a521e7420", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ad342a863590b24ce77681b7e081363fb3333f7 <57f7f1c6827be7d8f80feca48d2125fb91c6f6ed"}, {"id": "cbe4dedd-e325-3fe0-93bf-b05f313c092d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ad342a863590b24ce77681b7e081363fb3333f7 <44dab659064eb5c10adb0306510eebe848ed592d"}, {"id": "e526263c-7be3-394c-8d4b-6d822a8d4fbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "ebd06100-e810-3a0f-833b-dc5cdd7ad2e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ad342a863590b24ce77681b7e081363fb3333f7 <77906ac448d2fa81fa710ae26c0e591ebdc81154"}, {"id": "f7f32364-af71-3313-87e8-39567bb7616e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7558fb5f-8018-3ecb-ac73-4212291727a1", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}